From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 08:36:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: Flash A runtime fixes -- privapp allowlist,
 com.lge.os.Build stub, getSlotId redirect, permissive radio (bringup)

The com.lge.os.Build.CA_TARGET stub is what LG's stack uses to choose an IMS
profile: OperatorInfo reads OPERATOR and COUNTRY out of it and everything
downstream follows. Stock burns one value per SKU, which is right for a phone
that cannot change carrier core and wrong for a ROM that takes any SIM.

Hardcoding this device's "VZW" fails in a way that is painful to trace: the
VZW profile sends no Security-Client header, so a P-CSCF that wants RFC 3329
answers 421 Extension Required, Require: sec-agree, LG's stack does not retry,
and the phone has no VoLTE with nothing in the log saying 'wrong carrier'.
Calls fail LOCAL and SMS fails the same way.

So the stub derives both fields at class load, through
com.lge.ims.compat.CarrierTarget, from the properties the RIL maintains. It is
keyed on the serving network rather than the SIM, because an MVNO carries its
own MNC while riding the host's IMS core: Mint reads 310240 on the SIM and
310260 on the network, and T-Mobile's P-CSCF is the one that answers. That
covers every reseller on a mapped core without a row each. Roaming inverts it,
since IMS still belongs to the home operator, so the SIM wins there.

Mapped to the profiles the stack implements (VZW, TMO, ATT, SPR, MPCS) and
falling back to OPEN, LG's open market target, which ProviderDBUpdateHelper
compares TARGET_OPERATOR against, so it is a real value rather than a guess.
No Context is involved: these fields are read from a static initializer before
any Application exists, so properties are the only source available. Nothing
throws, because a throw there is ExceptionInInitializerError in a persistent
process.

persist.lg.ims.pref_operator still overrides all of it through
OperatorInfo.PREFERENCE_OPERATOR, which stays the escape hatch for a carrier
this mapping gets wrong.
